<title>EGYPT: Alex iron pays 10 pounds/share.</title>
<headline>Alex iron pays 10 pounds/share.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alexandria National Iron and Steel (ANSDK) has decided to pay a 10 pound dividend, and the equivalent for dollar shares, for the year ending December 31, 1996, a statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>The statement in Al-Ahram newspaper said the decision was taken at the shareholders meeting on March 2 and payment will start on April 1. The dividend was the same in 1995.</p>
<p>ANSDK shares closed on Cairo's bourse on Thursday at 247.25.</p>
<p>It was among the companies named by the Egyptian state to sell under its privatisation programme.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom 202 578-3290/1</p>
</text>
